# Live-Updates

The product runs on live machines. Ship only through Git `main`.

## Every shipped change

1. Read `MANIFEST.md` first (local, gitignored). Do not commit it.
2. Bump `server/version.py`, README version, TECHNICAL version.
3. Add a CHANGELOG entry. Update TECHNICAL if interfaces, ports, paths, or operations change.
4. Do not commit `data/` secrets, `projects/` user data, or `MANIFEST.md`.
5. Commit on `main`, then `git push origin main`. Fast-forward only. No force-push unless the user explicitly demands it.
6. Tell the user to update live systems with `./update.sh` or `update.bat` (or `git pull --ff-only origin main`, then pip, then restart).

## Do not

- Push to `master`
- Force-push `main`
- Mix local Test projects or PINs into git
- Skip the version bump for user-visible or live-deployed changes
